From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:59:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] conninfra: do not report suppressed status dumps

opfunc_therm_ctrl() rate-limits _status_dump() to one call every 10 s.
Each Wi-Fi/BT thermal query goes through it, and they come more often
than that, so __ratelimit() reports the calls it held back the next time
the window opens:

  opfunc_therm_ctrl: 1 callbacks suppressed

at KERN_WARNING, about six times a minute for the whole uptime. All it
held back is _status_dump(), which only prints at pr_debug, so the
summary is the one message in the path that does reach the log.

conninfra_core_thermal_query(), the caller that sends
CONNINFRA_OPID_THERM_CTRL, already sets RATELIMIT_MSG_ON_RELEASE on its
own ratelimit for the same reason. Do the same here.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [MediaTek vendor driver, exists only in the vendor tree]
---
 .../misc/mediatek/connectivity/conninfra/core/conninfra_core.c   | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/conninfra/core/conninfra_core.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/conninfra/core/conninfra_core.c
index bee2bb03938a..feb7b757f6ed 100755
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/conninfra/core/conninfra_core.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/conninfra/core/conninfra_core.c
@@ -803,6 +803,7 @@ static int opfunc_therm_ctrl(struct msg_op_data *op)
 
 	osal_unlock_sleepable_lock(&g_conninfra_ctx.core_lock);
 
+	ratelimit_set_flags(&_rs, RATELIMIT_MSG_ON_RELEASE);
 	if (__ratelimit(&_rs))
 		_status_dump();
 	conninfra_detect_time_change();
